==================================================
To compute the entropy of micellization (\Delta S), we use the thermodynamic relation:
\Delta S = \frac{\Delta H - \Delta G}{T}

Given:
* Temperature (T) = 298.15 \text{ K}
* Gibbs energy of micellization (\Delta G) = -27.271 \text{ kJ/mol} = -27,271 \text{ J/mol}

### Scenario (a)
* \Delta H = -5.0 \text{ kJ/mol} = -5,000 \text{ J/mol}
\Delta S_a = \frac{-5,000 - (-27,271)}{298.15} = \frac{22,271}{298.15} \approx 74.70 \text{ J/(mol}\cdot\text{K)}

### Scenario (b)
* \Delta H = +3.0 \text{ kJ/mol} = +3,000 \text{ J/mol}
\Delta S_b = \frac{3,000 - (-27,271)}{298.15} = \frac{30,271}{298.15} \approx 101.53 \text{ J/(mol}\cdot\text{K)}

